WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.237
Time: 4 minutes.

00:00:01.477 --> 00:00:11.084
Decide from the evidence: approve an accurate, eligible submission; reject an editable submitted sheet that needs correction under the local process;

00:00:11.084 --> 00:00:15.173
escalate unclear evidence or missing authority before deciding.

00:00:15.413 --> 00:00:20.363
In Fieldglass, rejection requires a reason and allows correction and resubmission.

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:23.077
The available route is configured locally.

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:28.781
For TS-104, use a factual reason that tells the submitter what to check.

00:00:29.021 --> 00:00:36.466
Strong sample: ‘For 5–9 October, compare Wednesday with the training record: 6 hours DEL and 2 TRN.

00:00:36.706 --> 00:00:40.589
Friday’s verified work record shows 6 DEL rather than 8.

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:44.285
Please correct and resubmit; expected total 38.’

00:00:44.975 --> 00:00:51.439
Why this works: it names the period, the two discrepancies, the supporting records, and the requested next step.

00:00:51.679 --> 00:01:01.737
It avoids personal criticism and does not expose unrelated information. ‘Wrong hours’ creates another round of clarification. ‘You padded your time’ makes an

00:01:01.737 --> 00:01:03.220
unsupported allegation.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:08.475
Before confirming a rejection, check that you are still in TS-104.

00:01:08.715 --> 00:01:11.745
In the sample, choose Reject and the precise reason.

00:01:11.985 --> 00:01:21.585
In a real tenant, use the approved reason category and comment fields your organization provides; do not assume the sample’s text is a configured category.

00:01:22.275 --> 00:01:33.965
Learner-authored practice (3 minutes): Write a 2–3 sentence rejection reason for synthetic TS-205, assignment NS-305, week 12–16 October.

00:01:34.205 --> 00:01:38.707
Tuesday shows 9 DEL but the verified record shows 7 DEL.

00:01:38.947 --> 00:01:45.432
Thursday totals 8 hours but should be split 6 DEL and 2 TRN, rather than 8 DEL.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.037
All other lines match.

00:01:47.277 --> 00:01:53.635
Identify the record and discrepancies, ask for correction and resubmission, and avoid assigning blame.

00:01:53.875 --> 00:01:56.563
Compare your text with the rubric before continuing.

00:01:57.253 --> 00:01:58.341
Now it's your turn.

00:01:58.581 --> 00:02:00.906
Choose the most useful rejection reason.

00:02:01.146 --> 00:02:04.261
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

